==English==

=== Etymology 1 ===
North America - a hawk mistakenly believed to regularly prey on chickens, possibly as justification for hunting the birds.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[chicken]] [[hawk]]}}

# {{context|obsolete|zoology}} Any of three North American [[hawk]] species ([[w:Cooper's Hawk|Cooper's Hawk]], [[w:Sharp-shinned Hawk|Sharp-shinned Hawk]], or [[w:Red-tailed Hawk|Red-tailed Hawk]]), mistakenly believed to be [[pest]]s.

=== Etymology 2 ===
Similar, under the OE sense of ''[[cycen]]'': young fowl.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[chicken]] [[hawk]]}}

# {{context|British|United State|gay|slang}} An [[adult]] male preferring younger male [[sexual partner]]s.

=== Etymology 3 ===
American English

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[chicken]] [[hawk]]}}

# {{context|pejorative|political|slang}} An advocate of [[war]] or military action who is avoiding personal [[military service]], or avoided it in the past.

